// Core v1 conformance — the autodiff leg.
//
// The suite differentiates this module's top level and pins the gradient IR
// the differentiator derives from the canonical primal, so a change to the
// autodiff surface fails the profile instead of passing unobserved.
//
// The program is deliberately a constant expression: it pins that the
// differentiator RUNS end-to-end from source and that its gradient module is
// byte-stable. Derivative correctness over tensor ops is pinned by the
// autodiff API tests (grad_of_square, grad_of_relu, matmul_rule_applied, ...);
// see the `deferred:` marker beside `cpu_cases()` in src/conformance.rs for
// why no source-level differentiable TENSOR program can be a cell yet.
2 * 5 + 4
